1
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:06,000
National Radio and Television Administration

2
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:30,000
[Pangjie Bathhouse Welcomes You]

3
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:35,520
What are you doing?

4
00:01:35,759 --> 00:01:37,520
You know what these things are,

5
00:01:37,520 --> 00:01:39,180
and you're throwing them out?

6
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:40,360
These are antiques.

7
00:01:40,360 --> 00:01:42,120
What antiques? It's a bunch of junk.

8
00:01:42,120 --> 00:01:44,440
Why did you have to move back?

9
00:01:44,440 --> 00:01:46,479
You're getting old. I'm here to keep you company.

10
00:01:46,479 --> 00:01:47,200
To take care of you in your old age.

11
00:01:47,200 --> 00:01:48,320
Do I need your company?

12
00:01:48,320 --> 00:01:49,720
Because I've been single for so many years,

13
00:01:49,720 --> 00:01:50,840
I'm used to being alone.

14
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:52,039
Suddenly having someone in the house,

15
00:01:52,039 --> 00:01:53,360
I'm not used to it.

16
00:01:53,360 --> 00:01:55,120
Then get used to it and deal with it.

17
00:01:55,120 --> 00:01:56,320
Tell me the truth.

18
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:57,840
Are you struggling right now?

19
00:01:57,840 --> 00:01:59,200
Are you out of money for rent?

20
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:00,400
What do you mean I have no money?

21
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:01,560
The truth is,

22
00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:02,960
it's close to my law firm.

23
00:02:02,960 --> 00:02:04,360
It makes my commute easier.

24
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:05,760
Don't just report the good news and hide the bad.

25
00:02:05,760 --> 00:02:07,480
If you weren't struggling, would you have sold your car?

26
00:02:07,480 --> 00:02:08,940
Would you have moved back?

27
00:02:10,280 --> 00:02:10,919
All right.

28
00:02:10,919 --> 00:02:12,400
We still have a mortgage on this house.

29
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:13,960
If you really can't manage, just sell the house.

30
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:14,960
Why would we sell the house?

31
00:02:14,960 --> 00:02:16,640
Stop worrying about money.

32
00:02:16,760 --> 00:02:18,120
No, if you're going to be like this,

33
00:02:18,120 --> 00:02:20,040
I have to find a job and make money.

34
00:02:20,079 --> 00:02:21,160
Just calm down.

35
00:02:21,520 --> 00:02:23,000
Do you know what the first rule is

36
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:24,120
of being Xiao Longnv's dad?

37
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:25,040
What?

38
00:02:25,040 --> 00:02:25,720
Don't ask,

39
00:02:25,960 --> 00:02:26,960
don't interfere,

40
00:02:27,040 --> 00:02:28,120
and just stay put.

41
00:02:30,720 --> 00:02:32,480
You...

42
00:02:32,680 --> 00:02:33,360
If you keep doing this,

43
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:34,560
I really can't take it anymore.

44
00:02:34,560 --> 00:02:36,520
What did I do to you that you can't take it?

45
00:02:36,520 --> 00:02:37,360
All right.

46
00:02:38,160 --> 00:02:39,290
Where are you going?

47
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:42,520
This...

48
00:02:50,880 --> 00:02:51,610
Stand still.

49
00:02:55,520 --> 00:02:57,320
What are you feeling guilty about now?

50
00:02:57,320 --> 00:02:59,180
Why are you reacting so strongly?

51
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:00,320
No, Chief Li.

52
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:01,800
What do you want?

53
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:02,720
You're retired,

54
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:04,040
and you still have this instinct.

55
00:03:04,040 --> 00:03:05,400
Are you using me to scratch that itch?

56
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:06,320
Isn't your conditioned reflex

57
00:03:06,320 --> 00:03:07,240
quite accurate?

58
00:03:07,240 --> 00:03:09,040
Look at your surrendering posture.

59
00:03:09,040 --> 00:03:10,040
It's so perfect.

60
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:11,880
All right, I forgive you.

61
00:03:11,880 --> 00:03:13,040
Keep me company. Let's go to your place for a drink.

62
00:03:13,040 --> 00:03:13,880
Let's go. Hurry.

63
00:03:13,880 --> 00:03:15,680
Drinking at this hour?

64
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:16,960
We have to celebrate.

65
00:03:16,960 --> 00:03:17,620
Celebrate?

66
00:03:17,760 --> 00:03:19,200
Xiaolong moved back.

67
00:03:19,440 --> 00:03:20,120
What?

68
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:21,800
Why did she move back?

69
00:03:22,040 --> 00:03:23,240
Is she short of money?

70
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:24,440
If she is, I have some.

71
00:03:24,440 --> 00:03:25,440
With her temper,

72
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:26,800
she wouldn't take your money even if you gave it to her.

73
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:28,040
I mean me.

74
00:03:28,360 --> 00:03:29,880
My good days are over.

75
00:03:30,160 --> 00:03:31,560
Won't she act like a warden

76
00:03:31,560 --> 00:03:33,320
and restrict my personal freedom every day?

77
00:03:33,320 --> 00:03:34,720
What freedom do you want?

78
00:03:34,880 --> 00:03:36,440
Do you want to break the law

79
00:03:36,600 --> 00:03:37,520
at home or something?

80
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:39,640
No, look at the sense of boundaries

81
00:03:39,640 --> 00:03:41,240
